<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huining (monk)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 664–665</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huining was a Chinese Buddhist monk from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> who sailed to the Javanese kingdom of Heling, known as Kalingga, in 664 or 665. There he worked with the local scholar Jnanabhadra to translate a Buddhist scripture on the Buddha's final nirvana into Chinese. His journey is recorded by the pilgrim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yijing">Yijing</a> as evidence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>'s role as a Buddhist centre.</p></div>
